  "footnote": [
   "CLANNAD: {CL_LINES} dialogue lines of a PS Vita playthrough (Vita3K), references read by Claude, Lens's cached readings of the same crops; Lens reads more lines exactly ({CL_LENS_EXACT}% vs {CL_N_EXACT}% for Normal).",
   "vita-test, psp-test: {VT_LINES} and {PT_LINES} hand-checked dialogue lines of {VT_GAMES} and {PT_GAMES} games (VNDB screenshots); every reader got the same crops, Lens in screen polarity. * Lens also reads the furigana the references omit: {PT_FUR_ERR} of its {PT_ALL_ERR} psp-test and {VT_FUR_ERR} of its {VT_ALL_ERR} vita-test errors (names included) fall on the {PT_FUR_LINES} and {VT_FUR_LINES} lines with furigana.",
   "Dialogue: lines without a speaker name. VOCR5: int8, plain-C runtime, greedy decoding; trained with the owner's captures, incl. planetarian, a Key / Prototype port like CLANNAD's. Time: estimated for a 3-line box on one Cortex-A9 core at 444 / 333 MHz; VOCR5 has not run on a console yet."
